[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The "vasa"]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.85]Lesson 27 | 第27课
[00:03.95]The 'Vasa' | “瓦萨”号
[00:12.34]What happened to the 'Vasa' almost immediately after she was launched? | “瓦萨”号下水后几乎立即遭遇了什么？
[00:20.57]From the seventeenth-century empire of Sweden, | 从17世纪瑞典的帝国讲起，
[00:24.32]the story of a galleon that sank at the start of her maiden voyage in 1628 must be one of the strangest tales of the sea. | 1628年首航伊始便沉没的一艘大帆船的故事，一定是海上最离奇的故事之一。
[00:34.84]For nearly three and a half centuries she lay at the bottom of Stockholm harbour until her discovery in 1956. | 它在斯德哥尔摩港的海底躺了将近三个半世纪，直到1956年才被发现。
[00:44.34]This was the Vasa, royal flagship of the great imperial fleet. | 这就是“瓦萨”号，大帝国舰队的皇家旗舰。
[00:51.53]King Gustavus Adolphus 'The Northern Hurricane', | 国王古斯塔夫斯·阿道弗斯——“北方飓风”——
[00:56.23]then at the height of his military success in the 'Thirty Years' War, | 当时正值他在“三十年战争”中战功赫赫的鼎盛时期，
[01:01.33]had dictated her measurements and armament. | 亲自规定了这艘船的规格和武器装备。
[01:05.42]Triple gun-decks mounted sixty-four bronze cannon. | 三层炮甲板上装着64门青铜加农炮。
[01:10.73]She was intended to play a leading role in the growing might of Sweden. | 它注定要在日益强大的瑞典王国中起主导作用。
[01:16.84]As she was prepared for her maiden voyage on August 10, 1628, Stockholm was in a ferment. | 1628年8月10日，当它准备首航时，斯德哥尔摩一片沸腾。
[01:27.58]From the Skeppsbron and surrounding islands | 人们从斯凯普斯布罗门码头和周围的岛屿上
[01:30.64]the people watched this thing of beauty begin to spread her sails and catch the wind. | 观看这件美丽的东西开始扬帆乘风。
[01:37.80]They had laboured for three years to produce this floating work of art; | 他们苦干了三年才造出这件漂浮的艺术品；
[01:44.16]she was more richly carved and ornamented than any previous ship. | 它比以往的任何船只都雕刻装饰得更华丽。
[01:50.09]The high stern castle was a riot of carved gods, demons, knights, kings, warriors, | 高耸的船尾楼上布满了雕刻的神、恶魔、骑士、国王、武士、
[01:58.90]mermaids, cherubs; and zoomorphic animal shapes ablaze with red and gold and blue, | 美人鱼、小天使以及闪烁着红金蓝色彩的动物形象，
[02:06.37]symbols of courage, power, and cruelty, | 这些象征勇气、权力和残酷的形象，
[02:10.57]were portrayed to stir the imaginations of the superstitious sailors of the day. | 是用来激发当时迷信的水手的想像力的。
[02:17.23]Then the cannons of the anchored warships thundered a salute to which the Vasa fired in reply. | 接着，停泊的战舰鸣炮向“瓦萨”号致礼，“瓦萨”号鸣炮答礼。
[02:25.64]As she emerged from her drifting cloud of gun smoke with the water churned to foam beneath her bow, | 当它从弥漫的炮烟中钻出来时，船首下翻腾着泡沫，
[02:32.92]her flags flying, pennants waving, sails filling in the breeze, | 旗帜飘扬，彩旗挥舞，海风中船帆渐渐张满，
[02:39.53]and the red and gold or her superstructure ablaze with colour, | 上层建筑的红金色彩闪闪发光，
[02:44.92]she presented a more majestic spectacle than Stockholmers had ever seen before. | 它呈现出的壮观景象是斯德哥尔摩人前所未见的。
[02:51.50]All gun-ports were open and the muzzles peeped wickedly from them. | 所有的炮门都开着，炮口不怀好意地从炮门里探出来。
[02:58.11]As the wind freshened there came a sudden squall and the ship made a strange movement, listing to port. | 风力增强时突然来了一阵狂风，船身奇怪地晃动了一下，向左舷倾斜。
[03:06.16]The Ordnance officer ordered all the port cannon to be heaved to starboard | 火炮军官命令把左舷的所有大炮移到右舷，
[03:11.68]to counteract the list but the steepening angle of the decks increased. | 以抵消倾斜，但甲板的陡度却在增加。
[03:18.28]Then the sound of rumbling thunder reached the watchers on the shore, | 这时，隆隆的雷鸣般的声音传到了岸上观者的耳中，
[03:22.91]as cargo, ballast, ammunition and 400 people went sliding and crashing down to the port side of the steeply listing ship. | 原来是货物、压舱物、弹药和400个人滑跌着、轰响着滚向严重倾斜的船的左舷。
[03:33.99]The lower gun-ports were now below water and the inrush sealed the ship's fate. | 下层炮门这时已在水下，涌进的海水注定了这艘船的命运。
[03:41.03]In that first glorious hour, the mighty Vasa, which was intended to rule the Baltic, | 在那壮丽的第一小时里，这艘本想称霸波罗的海的强大的“瓦萨”号，
[03:48.67]sank with all flags flying--in the harbour of her birth. | 旗帆齐张地沉没在了它诞生的港湾里。
